1
00:00:01,332 --> 00:00:06,607
(Q1) Official: Hello, Tourist Information Centre, Mike speaking, how can I help you?

2
00:00:06,607 --> 00:00:08,338
Woman: Oh, hi.

3
00:00:08,338 --> 00:00:11,121
[纵向表头1] I wanted to find out about cookery classes.

4
00:00:11,121 --> 00:00:15,012
I believe there are some one-day classes for tourists?

5
00:00:15,012 --> 00:00:19,598
Official: Well, they're open to everyone, but tourists are always welcome.

6
00:00:19,598 --> 00:00:22,367
OK, let me give you some details of what's available.

7
00:00:22,367 --> 00:00:24,241
There are several classes.

8
00:00:24,241 --> 00:00:29,292
[Example] One very popular one is at the Food Studio.

9
00:00:29,292 --> 00:00:35,790
[Q1答案句： choose。 空格【后】出现and] Official: They focus on seasonal products, and as well as teaching you how to cook them, they also show you how to choose them.

10
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:38,478
Woman: Right, that sounds good.

11
00:00:38,478 --> 00:00:40,499
(Q2) How big are the classes?

12
00:00:40,499 --> 00:00:43,912
[small 原词] Official: I'm not sure exactly, but they'll be quite small.

13
00:00:43,912 --> 00:00:53,834
[Q2答案句： 疑似答案出现要记录] Woman: And could I get a private lesson there?Official: I think so ... let me check, yes, they do offer those.

14
00:00:53,834 --> 00:00:58,997
Though in fact most of the people who attend the classes find it's a nice way of getting to know one another.

15
00:00:58,997 --> 00:01:01,755
(Q3) Woman: I suppose it must be, yes.

16
00:01:01,755 --> 00:01:09,957
[Q3答案句] Official: And this company has a special deal for clients where they offer a discount of 20 percent if you return for a further class.

17
00:01:09,957 --> 00:01:13,732
(Q4) Woman: OK. But you said there were several classes?

18
00:01:13,732 --> 00:01:15,226
Official: That's right.

19
00:01:15,226 --> 00:01:19,176
Another one you might be interested in is Bond's Cookery School.

20
00:01:19,176 --> 00:01:24,507
They're quite new, they just opened six months ago, but I've heard good things about them.

21
00:01:24,507 --> 00:01:31,599
[Q4答案句：healthy， A that is B = BA。 表头同替 concentrate on = focus] They concentrate on teaching you to prepare healthy food, and they have quite a lot of specialist staff.

22
00:01:31,599 --> 00:01:35,791
(Q5) Woman: So is that food for people on a diet and things like that?

23
00:01:35,791 --> 00:01:38,358
I don't know if I'd be interested in that.

24
00:01:38,358 --> 00:01:43,901
Official: Well, I don't think they particularly focus on low calorie diets or weight loss.

25
00:01:43,901 --> 00:01:54,428
[Q5答案句：build up=strengthen] It's more to do with recipes that look at specific needs, like including ingredients that will help build up your bones and make them stronger, that sort of thing.

26
00:01:54,428 --> 00:01:58,808
(Q6) Woman: I see. Well, I might be interested, I'm not sure.

27
00:01:58,808 --> 00:02:01,490
Do they have a website I could check?

28
00:02:01,490 --> 00:02:05,543
Official: Yes, just key in the name of the school - it'll come up.

29
00:02:05,543 --> 00:02:10,680
[Q6答案句：lecture] And if you want to know more about them, every Thursday evening they have a lecture at the school.

30
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:15,585
It's free and you don't need to book or anything, just turn up at 7:30.

31
00:02:15,585 --> 00:02:20,184
And that might give you an idea of whether you want to go to an actual class.

32
00:02:20,184 --> 00:02:23,943
(Q7) Official: OK, there's one more place you might be interested in.

33
00:02:23,943 --> 00:02:34,830
[Q7答案句] That's got a rather strange name, it's called The Arretsa Centre - that's spelled A-R-R-E-T-S-A.

34
00:02:34,830 --> 00:02:36,495
Woman: OK.

35
00:02:36,495 --> 00:02:39,205
(Q8) Official: They've got a very good reputation.

36
00:02:39,205 --> 00:02:45,825
[Q8答案句： mostly=mainly，specialize in = focus] They do a bit of meat and fish cookery but they mostly specialise in vegetarian dishes.

37
00:02:45,825 --> 00:02:50,689
Woman: Right. That's certainly an area I'd like to learn more about.

38
00:02:50,689 --> 00:02:53,224
(Q9) I've got lots of friends who don't eat meat.

39
00:02:53,224 --> 00:02:56,628
In fact, I think I might have seen that school today.

40
00:02:56,628 --> 00:03:00,379
[Q9答案句： 【记录疑似答案】一方提出，另一方肯定。 by = near] Is it just by the market?Official: That's right.

41
00:03:00,379 --> 00:03:03,294
So they don't have any problem getting their ingredients.

42
00:03:03,294 --> 00:03:04,580
They're right next door.

43
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:09,757
(Q10) [Q10答案句： 先记录疑似答案] And they also offer a special two-hour course in how to use a knife.

44
00:03:09,757 --> 00:03:15,317
They cover all the different skills - buying them, sharpening, chopping techniques.

45
00:03:15,317 --> 00:03:19,126
It gets booked up quickly though so you'd need to check it was available.

46
00:03:19,126 --> 00:03:22,292
Woman: Right, well thank you very much.

47
00:03:22,292 --> 00:03:24,792
I'll go and ...

